# Microsoft Agent Framework ↔ ADK (A2A) Interoperability Demo

This repository demonstrates Agent-to-Agent (A2A) interoperability between:

a Microsoft Agent Framework (Python) client agent using OpenAI, and

a Google ADK server-side agent exposed over A2A with an agent card.

The demo shows how a Microsoft agent can discover, connect to, and invoke a remote ADK agent via the A2A protocol, without either side sharing frameworks or models.

## Architecture Overview
┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Microsoft Agent Framework (Python)          │
│                                            │
│  ChatAgent (OpenAI)                         │
│    └── A2AAgent (remote tool) ───────────┐ │
│                                           │ │
└───────────────────────────────────────────┼─┘
                                            │  A2A (HTTP + Agent Card)
┌───────────────────────────────────────────┼─┐
│ Google ADK                                 │ │
│                                            │ │
│  A2A API Server                            │ │
│    └── check_prime_agent                   │◄┘
│        (Gemini or tool-only)               │
│        agent-card.json                     │
└────────────────────────────────────────────┘


The ADK agent acts as an A2A server

The Microsoft agent consumes the ADK agent as a remote tool

Communication happens via HTTP + agent card discovery

The two sides are fully decoupled

